        <body>
            <div xml:id="d540">

                <pb facs="0909" n="839" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg839"/>

                <head>No. 541.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis to Mr. Wallace.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 8,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 79.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 205, of the 12th ultimo,
                    touching the plan proposed by the Turkish minister of public instruction for
                    preventing future seizures of books of the American Bible Society, by affixing a
                    seal or stamp to them, has been received.</p>
                <p>Your note to the minister of foreign affairs upon the subject is approved, the
                    grounds upon which you base your present protest being concurred in by the
                    Department, and it is conceived to be essential that you should, as your note
                    indicates, receive more definite information in relation to the proposed measure
                    before finally giving your assent thereto.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN DAVIS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
